### Secure-VibeCode backend — manual test cheat-sheet
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy each block into curl.
###
### Ownership: POST /scans returns an X-Owner-Token response header. Every
### later request for that scan (GET, rescan, badge) must send it back as
### an X-Owner-Token request header, or you'll get a 404 -- same as if the
### scan didn't exist. Copy the token from the create response into
### {{ownerToken}} below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@ownerToken = paste-the-x-owner-token-header-value-here

### Create a scan
POST {{baseUrl}}/scans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "target": "https://github.com/example/lovable-app"
}

### Fetch a scan by id (replace {{scanId}} with the id from the response above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/scans/{{scanId}}
X-Owner-Token: {{ownerToken}}

### Rescan
POST {{baseUrl}}/scans/{{scanId}}/rescan
X-Owner-Token: {{ownerToken}}

### Check badge eligibility
GET {{baseUrl}}/scans/{{scanId}}/badge
X-Owner-Token: {{ownerToken}}

### Error case: missing scan
GET {{baseUrl}}/scans/does-not-exist
X-Owner-Token: {{ownerToken}}

### Error case: malformed create request
POST {{baseUrl}}/scans
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Error case: target isn't a valid URL -> 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/scans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "target": "not-a-url"
}

### Error case: correct scan id but no/wrong owner token -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/scans/{{scanId}}
X-Owner-Token: someone-elses-token
